{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116203","id":3276183531,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7DRpfr","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116203","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116203.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116203.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116203","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116203/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116203/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116203/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/f379b8400484cda50f245ab8fa07816950b96982","number":116203,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix `MaterialStorage::material_set_shader` race condition.","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #114896.\r\n\r\nAdds a mutex to protect the `data`, `type` and `owners` members of the `Shader` class.\r\n\r\nI think this minimal mutex usage should be enough for the following reasons (from my understanding):\r\n\r\nGetter and setter functions for shaders normally go through the `RenderingServer` command queue. The only exception is when a shader object is _just_ created and being set up. At that point, only the setup code references the object, so there is nothing to race against.\r\n\r\nAfter the initial setup, once the shader object can be referenced by materials, `material_set_shader` may manipulate the `owners` member concurrently. For this reason, we mandate a mutex lock for all accesses to `owners`.\r\n\r\nBesides that, `data` and `type` can be written by `shader_set_code` only in the command queue, while `material_set_shader` reads from them concurrently. So, we also add a mutex lock for these: when reading in `material_set_shader`, and when writing in `shader_set_code`.\r\n\r\nOther getters execute only in the `RenderingServer` command queue, so they cannot race with their writers.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what to assume for `shader_free`. Issues can happen if a shader is being freed while `material_set_shader` is accessing it, but I believe this always has been a theoretical problem? It doesn't appear to happen in practice.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repo